    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation on the `POST /api/owners` endpoint, following the existing read-time-derivation pattern used for fields like `locality` and `contactPreference`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `birthDate` (ISO date) input to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`) are code-generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `@Column(\"birth_date\")`) field with getter/setter so the value is persisted alongside `registrationDate`.\n\n3. **`mapper/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 A standalone helper (mirroring `OwnerLocality`) that computes whole-year age between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` via `ChronoUnit.YEARS.between`, returning `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), or `null` when no birth date is present.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Imported `AgeBand` and added an `ageBand` mapping expression that derives the band at read time from the stored `birthDate` against `registrationDate`.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run against `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the SQL).\n\nThe band is computed against the resolved (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` as the spec requires, and `ageBand` is omitted entirely when no `birthDate` is supplied.",
